.TH cgedit 1 "November 2026" "cgtools 1.4.0"
.\" one space after a full stop, not the sentence space roff adds
.ss 12 0
.SH NAME
cgedit \- a simple text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cgedit
.RI [ "toolkit options" ]
.RB [ \-\-codeset=\fICODESET\fP ]
.RB [ \-\-tab\-width=\fIWIDTH\fP ]
.RB [ \-\-jump=\fILINE\fP ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cgedit
edits one text file in a window that has menus and the text and nothing
else, as Leafpad does, and it does what Leafpad does: it reads and
writes files in other codesets than the locale's and finds out which a
file is in, undoes and redoes without limit, finds and replaces,
indents a new line as the one before it, numbers the lines, wraps them,
and takes files and text that are dropped on it. It does not print.
.PP
The window is called after the file. The name is in round brackets if
there is no such file yet, in angle brackets if the file cannot be
written, and has a star before it while the text is not as the file
has it.
.PP
A
.I file
that does not exist is a new file of that name, which is made when it
is first saved.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-codeset= CODESET
Read the file as text in this codeset, by any name that
.BR iconv (1)
knows, and do not find out.
.TP
.BI \-\-tab\-width= WIDTH
Make a tab this many spaces wide. It is 8 otherwise.
.TP
.BI \-\-jump= LINE
Put the cursor at this line of the file.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the options and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.PP
The toolkit's own options, such as
.BR \-\-display ,
are understood as well.
.SH MENUS
.SS File
.TP
.B New, Open, Save, Save As
The usual. If the text has changes that are not saved, it is asked
first whether to save them.
.B Open
and
.B Save As
ask for the codeset with the file:
.B Open
can find it out,
.B Save As
starts from the one the file was read in, and both offer the locale's,
UTF-8, those the locale's language has been written in, and
.BR "Other Codeset" ,
which takes any name
.BR iconv (1)
knows.
.B Save As
also asks how lines end: LF, CR+LF or CR. A file is saved with the
line ends it was read with.
.TP
.B Quit
Asks about changes that are not saved, and ends.
.SS Edit
.B Undo
and
.B Redo
go back and forth through everything done since the file was opened.
What is typed is undone a word at a time.
.BR Cut ,
.BR Copy ,
.BR Paste ,
.B Delete
and
.B Select All
are as everywhere. The same are in the menu the right button brings up.
.SS Search
.TP
.B Find
Asks what to find, and whether capitals matter. Every place it is at
is shown up, and the first after the cursor is selected.
.B Find Next
and
.B Find Previous
go on from there, and round the ends of the text.
.TP
.B Replace
Asks what to find and what to put in its place. Each place from the
cursor on is then gone to and asked about: Yes replaces it, No leaves
it, Cancel stops. With
.B Replace all at once
they are all replaced without asking, and undone together.
.TP
.B Jump To
Goes to a line by its number.
.SS Options
.TP
.B Font
Chooses the font of the text. Until one is chosen it is the theme's.
.TP
.B Word Wrap
Breaks a line that is wider than the window after its last word that
fits.
.TP
.B Line Numbers
Shows each line's number at its left.
.TP
.B Auto Indent
Starts a new line as far in as the one before it.
.PP
These and the window's size are kept for the next time.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Control+N, O, S, Q
New, Open, Save, Quit. Shift+Control+S is Save As.
.TP
.B Control+Z, Shift+Control+Z
Undo, Redo. Control+Y is Redo too.
.TP
.B Control+X, C, V, A
Cut, Copy, Paste, Select All.
.TP
.B Control+F, G, H, J
Find, Find Next, Replace, Jump To. Shift+Control+G is Find Previous.
.TP
.B Arrows, Home, End, Page Up, Page Down
Move the cursor; with Control, by words, to the ends of the text, and
so on; with Shift, select.
.TP
.B Tab, Shift+Tab
With more than one line selected, set the lines a tab further in, or
bring them back out.
.TP
.B Insert
Typing writes over what is there, until it is pressed again.
.TP
.B Control+Tab
Makes a tab four spaces wide, and eight again.
.TP
.B Control+T
Keeps the window above the others, and lets it be again, where the
desktop allows a window to ask for that.
.SH MOUSE
Press and drag selects; twice selects a word and three times a line;
Shift and a press selects from the cursor to there. The middle button
pastes what is selected, here or in another window. What is selected
can be dragged elsewhere in the text, where it is moved, or copied
with Control held, and to other programs. A file dropped on the window
is opened.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/cgedit/cgeditrc
The settings.
.I ~/.config
is used if
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is not set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iconv (1)
